FINAL ANSWER:
## Bus Factor Analysis
Period: all history (blame reflects current code) | Generated: 2026-10-24

**Short answer:** Felix Queißner wrote most of the code that matters. Felix is the last author of 772 of 2,120 lines (36%) and 64% of `src/args.zig`, the core library file. Losing Felix would leave the project's main file with no recently active author. The project-level bus factor is **2** by line-share, but that number hides the problem: the people still active can't cover half the code between them.

### Project-Level Bus Factor: 2

> Removing Felix alone leaves 64% of lines with other authors. Removing Felix and Wen Li (the next-largest owner) drops coverage below 50%, so two departures are needed. For `args.zig`, the answer is effectively 1.

I merged Felix's identities: 5 email addresses (`<email redacted>`, `<email redacted>`, `<email redacted>`, `<email redacted>`, `<email redacted>`) and 3 name spellings. This is an inference from matching names and emails. If you keep them separate, `<email redacted>` alone is still the largest single owner of `args.zig` (32%), but the concentration looks smaller.

### Overview

| Metric | Value |
|---|---|
| Source files (`.zig`) | 7 |
| Total lines analyzed | 2,120 |
| Lines last touched by Felix | 772 (36%) |
| Lines last touched by an author active in the last 90 days | 903 (43%) |
| Lines last touched by an author inactive for 90+ days | 1,217 (57%) |
| Active authors (commit since 2026-07-26) | 3: Wen Li, Tobias Ek, Dmitri Volkov |

Felix's last commit was 2026-04-16, about six months ago.

### Critical Risk Areas

| File | Lines | Main owner (share) | Owner active? | Dependents in repo | Risk |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `src/args.zig` | 1,049 | Felix (64%) | ❌ Felix inactive since Apr; only 5.5% of lines last touched by active authors | `demo.zig`, `demo_verb.zig`, plus external users of the library | **CRITICAL** |
| `src/width_table.zig` + `src/width.zig` | 508 | Wen Li (100%) | ✅ Last commit 2026-10-27 | None wired in yet (`width.zig` isn't imported) | HIGH (single author, but not yet used) |
| `src/help.zig` | 337 | Tobias Ek (100%) | ✅ Last commit 2026-10-21 | Imported by `args.zig` | HIGH (single author, active) |
| `demo.zig` | 63 | Felix (81%) | ❌ | Demo only | LOW |
| `demo_verb.zig` | 83 | Felix (47%), Vincent (17%) | ❌ | Demo only | MEDIUM |
| `build.zig` | 80 | Mochalins (28%), spread over 9 identities | ❌ No active author | Build | MEDIUM |

`args.zig` is the only file where a departure hurts the most. It has the most lines, the most history, and is the library's main API surface. Its active-author share is 5.5%, almost all of it from Wen Li (40 lines) and Dmitri Volkov (16 lines).

### Knowledge Distribution by Module

| Module | Contributors (identities) | Primary owner | Ownership % | Bus factor |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `src/args.zig` | ~20 | Felix | 64% | 1 (effective) |
| `src/help.zig` | 1 | Tobias Ek | 100% | 1 (active) |
| `src/width*.zig` | 1 | Wen Li | 100% | 1 (active) |
| `demo*.zig` | ~9 | Felix | 47–81% | 1 |
| `build.zig` | ~9 | Mochalins | 28% | 3+ (but all inactive) |

